-- pending: #172 (adapters over a generator of views of borrowed data, held across steps); first #686
-- now: 43:27: this argument of `filter` has type `1`, which is not `U pull A K R`
-- Hard problem 10: a pipeline of generator adapters over borrowed vectors. `views` yields a view
-- of each element of a borrowed vector; `filter` keeps the views whose element is above 2, `map`
-- turns the other vector's views into numbers, and `zip` pairs them. Each adapter holds its
-- source, and so the borrow, between steps, and `zip` holds a view it has pulled while it pulls
-- the other side. The `for` runs the pipeline inside the borrows of both vectors.
--
-- Issue: #172 (a borrow held across observations of codata), #682. `corpus/gen-borrowed.bc` pulls
-- a pipeline over a borrowed family by hand, because a `for` inside the borrow is a loop that
-- cannot keep the borrow (`corpus/reject/lend-iter-borrow.bc`, SPEC §14); its elements are copies.
--
-- Rust: `v.iter().filter(|x| **x > 2).zip(w.iter().map(|x| x * 10)).map(|(a, b)| a * b).sum()`;
-- every adapter is a struct bounded by `'a`, and the items are `&'a i32`.
--
-- Today: refused at the call of `views` passed to `filter` inside the borrow blocks: the call is
-- typed `1` there (#686: the same happens to `filter(upto(5), p)`, borrowing nothing, in a block
-- that has used its view). Both
-- backends stop at the same message. Iterating `views(vs)` directly in the block is refused
-- instead by SPEC §14 (the iterator holds the borrow; `corpus/reject/lend-iter-borrow.bc`).
--
-- Also needs: implicit copies of `imm` views (`corpus/pending/hard-imm-view-copy.bc`): this
-- program uses a view twice: `filter` hands each element to its predicate and then keeps it
-- (`corpus/pending/hard-filter-views.bc`).
--
-- Once it lands: i32[260]: 3 × 10 + 4 × 20 + 5 × 30; `live 0`.

include adapters

-- A view of each element of a borrowed vector.
fn views<'a>(xs: array_imm 'a i32) -> 1 with Yield[imm 'a i32] =
  for x in xs { yield(x) };
  ()

fn idx1(i: i32) -> i32 = i + 1

main -> i32 =
  let v = array_new[i32](5, idx1);
  let w = array_new[i32](3, idx1);
  let mut acc = 0;
  borrow imm v { 'a, vs ->
    borrow imm w { 'b, ws ->
      for p in zip(filter(views(vs), !{ x -> *x > 2 }), map(views(ws), !{ y -> *y * 10 })) {
        let (a, b) = p;
        acc = acc + *a * b
      } } };
  acc
